From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mingzq <north_sea@qq.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: rk3576: fix NULL bootdev deref in rk_board_dm_fdt_fixup

rk_board_dm_fdt_fixup() obtains the bootdev through android_get_bootdev()
when CONFIG_ANDROID_BOOTLOADER is enabled, but unlike fit.c and vendor.c
it lacks a fallback to rockchip_get_bootdev(). On non-Android boots (e.g.
Armbian booted from NVMe), android_get_bootdev() always returns NULL, so
the following "desc->if_type" dereference raises a Synchronous Abort
(data translation fault) right before jumping to the kernel.

Add the same android -> rockchip_get_bootdev() fallback used by fit.c and
vendor.c, plus a final NULL guard that simply skips the UFS fixup (harmless
on NVMe boot, where no UFS device is present). Fixes the boot crash seen
on reComputer RK3576 DevKit with secure-boot + A/B OTA.

Signed-off-by: Ming Zhangqun <north_sea@qq.com>
---
 arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rk3576/rk3576.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rk3576/rk3576.c b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rk3576/rk3576.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rk3576/rk3576.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/rk3576/rk3576.c
@@ -425,12 +425,17 @@ int rk_board_dm_fdt_fixup(const void *blob)
 {
 #ifdef CONFIG_ANDROID_BOOTLOADER
 	struct blk_desc *desc = android_get_bootdev();
+	if (!desc)
+		desc = rockchip_get_bootdev();
 #else
 	struct blk_desc *desc = rockchip_get_bootdev();
 #endif
 	const char *status = NULL;
 	int node = -1;
 
+	if (!desc)
+		return 0;
+
 	/*
 	 * 1. Kernel DTS will enable UFS by default.
 	 *
-- 
